LOGBOOK.md:1532:- FIX (B2): `TestDecodeQueryAllOperationsAdmit` drives 17/17 registry operations (was 5/17); 40+ validator defects through DecodeQuery including the review probes environments/"root", jobs/"pwned", distinct/"secret" (battery V01–V03, all killed). Zero functions at 0.0% (was 10, all §10.8.5 validators).
LOGBOOK.md:1544:- FINDINGS: (1) §10.8.5 prose names `query_cursor_mismatch` but the pinned error registry does not register it — cursor reuse refuses as `query_invalid` with a cursor-mismatch detail. (2) The response envelope carries its own `schema` + `schema_version` (1.0.0 both majors): the downgrade tuple names a response schema_version no schemaless reading can carry. (3) `node manifest is not canonical JSON` is reachable, not defensive: extensions values cross opaquely while the canonicalizer enforces depth 256 (300-deep vector proves it). (4) `failCapability` removed — no entry point in this deliverable raises `capability_unavailable`; the taxonomy test pins the 8 emitted codes instead of keeping a dead constructor for census symmetry.
LOGBOOK.md:1596:- FIX (F1r): the nine membership-checked vocabularies with no derivation (manifest/probe/capability/identity/identify/quiesce/spawn/status member sets plus the yolo mapping) are now derived from the pinned document — example-JSON keys for 7.3/7.4, first-sentence code spans for the capability-value sentence, TableRowAt Field rows for the 5.5 identity table, per-span member declarations for the 7.5 SpawnPlan/SafeBoundaryProof/ProviderTransactionStatus rows, braced-cell parsing for the identify-session success body, per-row provider-plus-first-flag for the 7.7 table. The census parses production source for package-level []string/map[string]bool/map[string]string with membership use (unknownMember argument, map index, range operand) and requires each of the 19 found vocabularies to carry an executing derivation, in both directions.
LOGBOOK.md:1604:- FIX (F1, blocking): the eight closed vocabularies the three existing specdoc derivations did not cover are now derived the same way in `internal/provhost/closed_vocabularies_test.go` — probe statuses and evidence from the Section 7.4 sentences, architectures from 7.4 prose cross-checked against the 7.5 probe request row, probe platforms from that row (sorted both sides: the row lists macos first, the implementation holds sorted order), quiesce blockers from the 7.5 enum sentence, identity kinds from the 5.5 table row, identify confidence and matched-evidence from the 7.5 identify-session row. Each widening mutant from the verdict battery (partial, assumed, 386, freebsd, other, legacy_alias, guess, guessed) is killed twice: once by the derivation equality, once by an exact-member refusal row through the production entry point.
LOGBOOK.md:1609:- FIX (F6): aliasing tests for both copy guarantees (`MutationOperations`, `Capabilities`); the quiesce safe-rule comment restated to name backgroundNull as folded into !background by `rawNullableBool` (unreachable, not untested); the vacuous `runner.spawned() != 0` assertion on a Runner never handed to `RequireCapability` removed and restated as structural.
LOGBOOK.md:1617:- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti (final leaf of STORY-260830-3jqsx1). New `internal/provhost` operation layer: manifest (7.3), probe + capability gate (7.4/8.3), profile mapping (7.7), quiescence proof (7.6), SpawnPlan for launch/resume, Provider Identity Record + identify result (5.5), and the single `(operation, operation_id)` key (7.5), with Host.Call conformance sequences (manifest/probe/resume/identify/quiesce end to end, 21 fail-closed capability-by-status tuples with zero processes started, byte-identical lost-prepare retry, changed-body `idempotency_mismatch` passthrough, child-code passthrough table). Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.
LOGBOOK.md:1648:- FINDING: the §7.3/§7.5 operation registry counts 15, not 16 — the manifest JSON and the §7.5 table both list manifest, probe, launch, identify-session, quiesce, native-store-plan, capture, materialize, materialize-status, materialize-commit, materialize-rollback, resume, fork, stop, doctor. The ownership gap prose saying "16-entry" miscounts; the registry test derives the 15 from the pinned table in order.
LOGBOOK.md:1668:- SCOPE: TASK-260830-1zvmw7 rework after CHANGES REQUESTED (F1–F5, F9, G-A blocking; F6–F8 non-blocking). Production: `CheckOperation` admits `manifest`/`probe` with no capability dependency (§4.D); dead probe-identity branch and subsumed platform-dup check removed; `checkEvidenceSet` doc corrected to whole-reconciliation refusal. Tests: every refusal assertion in `manifest_test.go`/`manifest_pin_test.go` now names `*Error.Detail` (was 0/29); four over-determined `TestReconcileRefusals` fixtures narrowed until only the named rule rejects; `ParseProbe`/`ParseEvidence` gain the schema/version/identity/kind/digest cases only `ParseManifest` had; `now == expires_at` boundary row added.
LOGBOOK.md:1670:- F1 (live spec violation): `CheckOperation("manifest"|"probe")` refused `terminal_backend_capability_unproven` even fully admitted; §4.D gives both `Capability dependencies: none` and neither row allows that code. Pinned by `TestCheckOperationAdmitsDependencyFreeOperations` (empty + full admitted sets, plus the still-refused gated operation).
LOGBOOK.md:1700:- SCOPE: new `internal/terminalbackend/` (registry, canonical IDs, version tuples, trust, duplicate/drift refusal, restore binding, §7.A descriptor check), `internal/config/validation.go` wiring, new `internal/config/terminal_registry_wiring_test.go`. TASK-260830-2xdt8t, spec v0.5.0 §4.B, §4.1, §6.5, §7.A. Signed commit on story branch, worktree clean, not pushed.
LOGBOOK.md:1786:- ROOT CAUSE: `README.md` published "73 executable acceptance cases" while `ownership.v0.5.0.json` held 74 entries with 74 distinct ids and `tracecheck` printed `acceptance_cases=74`. The first pass of this leaf moved the registry from 65 to 73 and updated the sentence; the round-2 rework added a case and did not. Nothing measured the figure — setting it to 999 left `go test ./...` and `tracecheck` both at exit 0.
LOGBOOK.md:1930:- FINDING: M6 is what separates a stated bound from a held one. The graph resolves a computed callee to every function whose identifier is used as a value in the package, so the derived entry-point set is exact *only while* `validateAXNumbers` is never used as a value. That precondition is not narration — it is the single test standing between a dispatch-table registration and a silently widened set with the whole suite `ok`.
LOGBOOK.md:1974:- ROOT CAUSE: the clause anchor holds a citation to the right numbered section; it cannot hold it to the right row of a table that declares several sibling schemas one per line. `SPEC.md:4787-4793` declares seven Git types one table row each, all in Section 10.4. Seven shipped enumeration rows cited a sibling's row: `GitIndex.format` quoted GitObjectPack's `format:git_pack_v2` while `validateGitIndex` (`closed_shapes.go:1454`) enforces `git_index`; `GitIndexEntry.mode` quoted GitHead's `mode:branch|detached|unborn` while `closed_shapes.go:1514` enforces `requireUint(object, "mode", 1<<32-1)`; `GitIndexEntry.oid` quoted GitHead's nullable `oid` while `requireGitOID` admits no null. Every rule then in place admitted them — verbatim text, correct line, correct clause, member name present as a substring — and `go test ./... -count=1` exited 0 with all seven shipped.
LOGBOOK.md:1979:- EVIDENCE: 14 sibling retargets derived from the document itself — every shared-member pair of the Section 10.4 Git table, both directions — each planted into a copy of the shipped artifact and each required to be refused by the sibling's name. Six mutants run in a throwaway `git archive` copy, all confirmed present before measurement: deleting the anchor reddens all 15 sibling and field plants; narrowing it to `Type` tables only reddens the field-table plant; restoring one of the seven pre-fix citations reddens and names the row and GitHead; removing the table-row boundary reddens both the specdoc and the artifact stitch tests; removing one declaring pin reddens 8 shipped rows rather than granting a free pass; a stale pin and a stale exemption both redden. Class re-scan over all 347 rows: 357 citations, 235 on table body rows, 0 naming another type, 2 naming another member and both exempted by name.
LOGBOOK.md:1996:- NOTE: the residual limit is stated in the artifact and `README.md` rather than left implied. The anchor is a clause, not a shape — ten shapes are declared in 10.4 — so a retarget *within* a clause is still admitted, and `strings.Contains(text, row.member)` still matches a member name embedded in another schema's identifier. The `environment_id` case sits inside that gap: both of its lines are in 7.8.
LOGBOOK.md:2060:- ROOT CAUSE of the consequence: a fragment was installed into quarantine and reported with `PutResult.Digest`/`Size` describing bytes no artifact on disk held — the digest of the full source attached to a truncated file. An incident record built from that result would name a digest that does not match the quarantined bytes. Second consequence: a full volume made the store write MORE data, into quarantine, on the volume whose exhaustion caused the fault.
LOGBOOK.md:2114:- DECISION, an over-refusal declined: parent directories are NOT required to be declared. SPEC.md §10.4/§13.14 states no such rule, and the shipped `transferManifestWithEntries(count)` fixture already declares `p/00000` with no `p` entry. Overlap is also compared bytewise, not case-folded — folding does not preserve byte order, so the stack cannot run over folded paths — and that narrowing is disclosed in the artifact row rather than silently assumed.
LOGBOOK.md:2131:- FINDING: `testdata/closed-vocabularies.md` pins the admitted set of all 47 production vocabulary call sites and kills any widening mutant at the source. It says nothing about WHICH member each gate is reached from. A validator that read a Lease Record `reason` through the `session.quiescing` reason gate would leave every pinned row byte-identical while admitting `stop` on a lease. The pin is over the source, the defect is over the wiring.
LOGBOOK.md:2133:- ANOMALY, and the reason the first version of this sweep was worthless: keying the declared set by member NAME let the widening mutant through. `reason` is declared twice — Lease Record `{create, graceful_takeover, force_takeover, recovery}` and `session.quiescing` `{graceful_takeover, stop, checkpoint}` — so the member-name union already contained `stop` and the sweep never substituted it. Mutant M3 SURVIVED the first run. Same shape for `kind` (session vs Transfer Manifest) and `materialization_policy` (git vs managed_tree member).
LOGBOOK.md:2142:- FINDING: mutating `validateCommonRecordEnvelope` to skip its `created_by_host_id` check when the member is ABSENT survives both the new Section 10.1 provenance sweep and the whole existing package suite. Every Section 10.1 validator calls `requireExactMembers` with its closed member list BEFORE `validateIdentityRecordEnvelope`, so an object missing the member is refused as an incomplete member set and the mutated branch is never executed at either identity production entry. Equivalent mutant, not an evidence gap.
LOGBOOK.md:2222:- FINDING: reproduced against OpenSSH 10.2p1 on this host — `ssh -G -vo StrictHostKeyChecking=no` prints `stricthostkeychecking false` (grouped short flags were never seen), `-o StrictHostKeyChecking=false` and `=NO` also print `false` (live aliases, case-folded), and `-F`, `ProxyCommand`, `KnownHostsCommand`, `Include`, `PermitLocalCommand`+`LocalCommand` were unknown to the filter entirely.
LOGBOOK.md:2229:- REAPPLY: this leaf was reprovisioned onto a fresh Story workspace after an empty-OID checkpoint; the accepted patch was reapplied rather than reimplemented, and every gate and mutant below was rerun in the new workspace instead of inherited from the earlier run. The five cited OpenSSH behaviours were reproduced again against the live OpenSSH 10.2p1 binary on this host.
LOGBOOK.md:2398:- FINDING: That blind spot is why a real defect reached review — `internal/canonicaljson/core_records.go` `validateTerminalV4Payload` validated `terminal_backend_id` with `requireString` only, so `CalculateObjectIdentity` attested `AX.TMUX`, `../../etc/passwd`, an embedded NUL and 5000 chars. SPEC.md:890 (§4.B) pins it to 1–128 ASCII bytes matching `[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:[.-][a-z0-9]+)*`.
LOGBOOK.md:2422:- FINDING (F1): The refusal-arm derivation walked FuncDecl bodies only, so a package-level `var f = func() *Error {…}` arm and an aliased constructor (`refuse := mismatchf`) each shipped reachable with a new detail while both inventory tests stayed green. Both shapes measured empty in the tree, so the 193/193 ratio held while the closure claim did not.
