  1374	### 4.1 Terminal backend interface
  1375	
  1376	Every terminal backend MUST implement these semantic operations:
  1377	
  1378	| Operation | Required result |
  1379	| --- | --- |
  1380	| <code>create</code> | With <code>session_id</code> and caller-stable <code>bootstrap_operation_id</code>, create a durable pane/process whose only stable entry point is <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>. |
  1381	| <code>attach</code> | Connect an operator to the local terminal without changing ownership. |
  1382	| <code>status</code> | Report process presence, wrapper state, provider child state, and attachability. |
  1383	| <code>quiesce-input</code> | Stop new operator/provider input while retaining observation. |
  1384	| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | Prove the adapter-specific safe boundary or time out. |
  1385	| <code>request-stop</code> | Ask the provider to exit through a version-tested graceful path. |
  1386	| <code>terminate-stale</code> | Terminate a process only for explicit force recovery after preserving diagnostics. |
  1387	| <code>restore</code> | Recreate the wrapper after reboot and consult current ownership before any provider resume. |
  1388	
  1389	The wrapper MUST validate configuration, load the logical session, synchronize
  1390	known lease records when possible, and compare the local fencing token before
  1391	launching a provider. It MUST park safely when ownership is remote, ambiguous,
  1392	or unverified.
  1393	
  1394	Terminal creation and the wrapper's first child start are idempotent on
  1395	<code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code>. The backend MUST durably bind
  1396	that pair before child creation. An identical retry returns or reattaches to
  1397	the one recorded wrapper/child; changing the operation for a session still in
  1398	the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. After a lost result,
  1399	<code>status</code> plus that binding MUST prove absence or identify the one
  1400	child before any start retry. This contract never persists or replicates a PID
  1401	as identity.
  1402	
  1403	### 4.2 tmux backend
  1404	
  1405	On macOS, Linux, and WSL2, the supported durable terminal backend is tmux. Every
  1406	managed pane MUST run:
  1407	
  1408	~~~shell
  1409	ax pane <logical-session-id>
  1410	~~~
  1411	
  1412	It MUST NOT run the raw provider command as the pane's stable command.
  1413	<code>tmux-resurrect</code> plus <code>tmux-continuum</code> MAY recreate local
  1414	tmux layout and invoke the wrapper after reboot. They MUST NOT be described or
  1415	used as cross-host migration.
  1416	
  1417	AX MUST use its dedicated <code>-S</code> server and MUST NOT discover or reuse
  1418	the operator's default tmux server by ambient socket name. On macOS, server
  1419	creation is credential-sensitive. A Background caller MUST NOT create a
  1420	credential-dependent tmux server. A background CLI, SSH RPC process, daemon,
  1421	or restore worker MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua broker and
  1422	its attested AX tmux server; if neither exists it MUST return
  1423	<code>capability_unavailable</code> with typed realm/readiness details and MUST
  1424	NOT fall back to direct server creation.
  1425	
  1426	<code>launchctl managername</code> is a diagnostic hint only. Conformance
  1427	requires a functional AX sentinel inside the exact tmux server plus a separate
  1428	provider-auth smoke using the selected provider. Evidence MUST bind the exact
  1429	tmux server generation, provider build, and macOS version. Aqua alone and
  1430	sentinel-only evidence are insufficient. Any provider flow requiring GUI
  1431	interaction, Keychain UI, a permission prompt, or other human action fails
  1432	closed until that interaction succeeds in the verified GUI realm.
  1433	
  1434	After restore, the wrapper MUST:
  1435	
  1436	1. read the latest locally known lease;
  1437	2. attempt a mesh lease refresh without blocking forever;
  1438	3. resume locally only if the local host has the winning lease and the required
  1439	   materialization is valid;
  1440	4. offer remote attach/takeover when another host owns the session in an
  1441	   interactive terminal; or
  1442	5. enter <code>parked</code> without launching the provider in all other cases.
  1443	
  1444	Logout or reboot invalidates unrenewed realm evidence. Without a verified GUI
  1445	realm, recovery MUST remain parked until GUI login re-establishes the broker,
  1446	functional sentinel, provider-auth smoke, and their generation/build/version
  1447	binding. A cached sentinel or prior <code>managername</code> observation MUST
  1448	NOT authorize resume.
  1449	
  1450	### 4.3 Native Windows backend
  1451	
  1452	Native Windows PowerShell MUST use a Windows terminal backend implemented with
  1453	Go process supervision and ConPTY. It MUST support mesh sync, workspace and
  1454	provider materialization, direct/provider resume, task-board open/adopt, remote
  1455	attach, graceful takeover when the provider row passes ConPTY gates, force
  1456	takeover, stop, and continuation.
  1457	
  1458	Native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux or tmux resurrection. A reboot destroys the
  1459	live ConPTY. The user service MUST recreate <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>,
  1460	which resumes from the latest valid checkpoint only after lease validation.

