  4600	### 10.2 Content-addressed blobs
  4601	
  4602	A blob is an uninterpreted byte sequence identified by SHA-256. Blob metadata
  4603	MUST live in a manifest, not in the blob path. Before publishing a record that
  4604	references a blob, the writer MUST fsync the blob, verify its size and digest,
  4605	and atomically install it in the object store.
  4606	
  4607	Provider/task-board blobs can contain sensitive project history. Logs and
  4608	metrics MUST record digest, size, and media type only, never blob contents.
  4609	
  4610	Every transferred blob has a Blob Descriptor with schema
  4611	<code>urn:ax:schema:blob</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Chunks MUST be
  4612	sorted, contiguous, non-overlapping, start at offset zero, and cover exactly
  4613	<code>size</code> bytes:
  4614	
  4615	The descriptor is closed and contains exactly
  4616	<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,
  4617	<code>descriptor_id:digest</code>, <code>blob_id:digest</code>,
  4618	<code>size:uint53</code>, <code>media_type:string[1..255]</code>, and
  4619	<code>chunks:BlobChunk[0..32768]</code>. <code>media_type</code> is a lowercase
  4620	ASCII <code>type/subtype</code> without parameters. BlobChunk is closed and
  4621	contains exactly <code>index:uint32</code>, <code>offset:uint53</code>,
  4622	<code>size:uint53[1..4194304]</code>, and <code>chunk_id:digest</code>. Indexes
  4623	start at zero and increase by one. An empty blob has size zero and no chunks;
  4624	a non-empty blob has at least one.
  4625	
  4626	~~~json
  4627	{
  4628	  "schema": "urn:ax:schema:blob",
  4629	  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  4630	  "descriptor_id": "sha256:390c8f21900483a010c1cbc3f9be01afebcf6e4da87263ba09fc5776dd6503ee",
  4631	  "blob_id": "sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50",
  4632	  "size": 11,
  4633	  "media_type": "application/octet-stream",
  4634	  "chunks": [
  4635	    {
  4636	      "index": 0,
  4637	      "offset": 0,
  4638	      "size": 11,
  4639	      "chunk_id": "sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50"
  4640	    }
  4641	  ]
  4642	}
  4643	~~~
  4644	
  4645	The descriptor ID is its canonical object digest with
  4646	<code>descriptor_id</code> omitted. The example describes the eleven raw bytes
  4647	<code>ax-example\n</code>, whose unpadded base64url form is
  4648	<code>YXgtZXhhbXBsZQo</code>; the one last-chunk digest therefore equals the
  4649	whole-blob digest. Empty blobs have an empty chunk array. Protocol 1.0.0 permits
  4650	at most 32,768 chunks in one Blob Descriptor, so one blob is at most 128 GiB.
  4651	A larger file MUST fail capture with <code>capability_unavailable</code> before
  4652	publishing a partial manifest.
  4653	
  4654	### 10.3 Transfer Chunk Descriptor
  4655	
  4656	The transfer unit is a fixed 4 MiB chunk except the last chunk. Chunk schema is
  4657	<code>urn:ax:schema:chunk</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>:
  4658	
  4659	The Transfer Chunk Descriptor is closed and contains exactly
  4660	<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,
  4661	<code>blob_id:digest</code>, <code>index:uint32</code>,
  4662	<code>offset:uint53</code>, <code>size:uint53[1..4194304]</code>, and
  4663	<code>chunk_id:digest</code>. It has no extension map. Offset MUST equal index
